# The container image a released ref runs, so a released ref knows its own image.
#
# `.github/workflows/release.yml` writes this file on the release commit it creates, after it has
# built the image and pushed it to ghcr.io, and then points `v<version>` and `v1` at that commit.
# That is the whole reason the file exists: `uses: aicodesentry/mitig8it/action@v1` checks out the
# repository at the tag, so whatever this file says at that commit is what the action pulls, with
# no registry lookup and nothing to resolve at run time.
#
# On `main`, on any branch, and in a fork the three values below are empty, and that is correct
# rather than incomplete. An unreleased ref has no published image to name, so `action.yml` builds
# from source there, which is the behaviour every ref had before this file existed.
#
# `action.yml` parses these lines with `sed`; it never sources the file. A released ref should not
# be able to run shell in the caller's runner merely by being checked out, and every value is
# checked against a regex before it reaches a `docker pull` argument.
#
# MITIG8IT_VERSION        the released semantic version, with no leading `v`, e.g. 1.0.0
# MITIG8IT_IMAGE          the image repository, without a tag or a digest
# MITIG8IT_IMAGE_DIGEST   the manifest digest ghcr.io returned for that push, sha256:<64 hex>

MITIG8IT_VERSION=
MITIG8IT_IMAGE=
MITIG8IT_IMAGE_DIGEST=
